  "description": "Participants see pictures of ten interior materials (wall paint, textile, wood, plastic, glass, metal, tile, brick, stone, concrete) in random order and rate each on the study's 12 adjective pairs (1–7) chosen for the four restorative features: being away, extent, fascination and compatibility. Rebuilt from Zhao, Nagai, Gao, Shen & Fan (2023), IJERPH 20(14): 6364, with the paper's Figure 1 pictures (CC BY 4.0). Scoring as in the paper: mean of each feature's pairs; preference = fascination + compatibility; relaxation = being away + compatibility; restorative potential = sum of all four; Wilcoxon signed-rank tests for the 45 material pairs.",
